{
  "_comment": "See worlds/templates/CHARACTER_ASSET_SPEC.md. Contemporary city dress, drawn in the four isometric headings like the Chang'an cast. COMPLETE: all eight gender x age sheets are drawn, each carrying the full 76-frame contract. Three known deviations from spec 1.2, all measured against the shipped Chang'an cast as the reference rather than against the spec's numbers alone: (1) DYE — these sheets paint their garments at median value 0.11-0.33 where the shader re-lights against ART_LIT = 0.70 (recolorPipeline.ts), so every identity colour renders at roughly a fifth to a half of its intended value; Chang'an's sheets sit at 0.42-0.56, so this is a property of this cast, not of the constant. Uniform across all eight, so it reads as a dark-clothed city rather than as a fault, but two agents of adjacent colours are harder to tell apart here. (2) MIDDLE — spec asks the middle bracket for young's height with a torso ~8% WIDER; both middle sheets are 10-13% NARROWER instead, so at the 0.28 draw scale middle is not distinguishable from young. Chang'an misses this one too (7-11% narrow), so it is a requirement no cast has yet met rather than a fault of this one. (3) ELDER — the stoop is meant to shorten the silhouette (Chang'an's elders stand 5% below its young, spec 54px vs 57px); these elders measure the same height as young, so the bracket's most important signal is not carried. Re-draws are welcome; none of the three stops the map rendering.",
